<header class="page-header wrap narrow">
  <p class="eyebrow">About the game</p>
  <h1>A living world, and the spirit who watches over one people</h1>
  <p class="lede">LivingWorld is a fantasy simulation set in a generated world that develops on its own. You guide a single band of people across generations, from a few dozen wanderers to whatever they become.</p>
</header>

<section class="wrap narrow prose">
  <h2>The premise</h2>
  <p>You are not the chief. You are the band’s <strong>ancestral spirit</strong>. Leaders are mortal and come and go, but you remain. You can instruct a leader directly, take their advice, or hand whole responsibilities over to them. Instructions still have to work in the real world. People need food and time, tools need materials, and scouts can lose their way.</p>
  <p>The world doesn’t revolve around you. Other bands follow the same rules and make their own choices. They migrate, split apart, find new resources and learn new crafts whether you are watching or not.</p>

  <h2>How a game begins</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Generate a world.</strong> The geography, rivers, forests and resources shape everything that follows.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose a people:</strong> Human, Dwarf, Elf or Goblin.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose a band</strong> from the communities that actually exist in that world.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose a leader</strong> from real members of that band, then begin on Day 0.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Your band might stay small and free. It might become hunters, crafters, traders or raiders, or settle down and grow into something much larger. Nothing in the game picks that path for you.</p>
</section>

