<section class="wrap narrow prose">
  <h2>What exists today</h2>
  <p>LivingWorld is early, and most of the work so far has gone into the simulation underneath. Here is what runs today:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A generated world that the simulation advances one day at a time, through 365-day years and four seasons.</li>
    <li>Bands of all four peoples that gather, hunt, keep animals, migrate and sometimes split into new communities.</li>
    <li>Named characters such as leaders, scouts and crafters who grow out of each band’s real members.</li>
    <li>Scouting expeditions that bring back reports of what they actually saw, including when they are unsure.</li>
    <li><strong>Craft Circles</strong>, small groups of crafters who make tools, teach newcomers and pass their knowledge on.</li>
    <li>A playable prototype with a map of the world, the Day-0 choice of people, band and leader, and leaders who bring decisions to you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The 3D camp and the polished interface in the images on this site are <strong>concept art</strong>. They show where the game is heading, not what it looks like today. Real screenshots and footage will appear in the <a href="/devlog/">devlog</a> as they become worth showing.</p>
</section>

